272
00:17:29,260 --> 00:17:32,160
the link, and I'll wait
until you... Welcome

273
00:17:41,110 --> 00:17:43,510
back. Here's another
look at the major

274
00:17:43,510 --> 00:17:45,990
proteins encoded
by the HIV genome.

275
00:17:46,210 --> 00:17:50,190
We've talked about GAG,
POLL, and ENV. There are

276
00:17:50,190 --> 00:17:52,650
also other genes that
are not within the main

277
00:17:52,650 --> 00:17:55,570
reading frames, some of
them discontinuous, and

278
00:17:55,570 --> 00:17:59,210
even one, NEF, within
a long-terminal repeat.

279
00:17:59,270 --> 00:18:03,250
These proteins elegantly
give HIV an advantage

280
00:18:03,250 --> 00:18:06,310
over the host cell by
decreasing host cell

281
00:18:06,310 --> 00:18:09,270
defenses and preventing
the expression of CD4

282
00:18:09,270 --> 00:18:11,610
receptors on the surface
by degrading them

283
00:18:11,610 --> 00:18:16,470
intracellularly, and the
product of the NEF gene, the

284
00:18:16,470 --> 00:18:19,210
one that's in the three
-prime long-term repeat,

285
00:18:19,750 --> 00:18:25,870
down regulates both CD4 and
MHC1 expression, resulting

286
00:18:25,870 --> 00:18:29,590
in an infected T helper
cell's inability to bind

287
00:18:29,590 --> 00:18:33,570
both antigen-presenting
cells or to bind antigen

288
00:18:33,570 --> 00:18:37,770
itself, preventing the T
cell's activation. Oh, and

289
00:18:37,770 --> 00:18:41,790
for those of you who did
not look at that video on

290
