294
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:07,960
Here's how HIV infects
cells. The virion binds to

295
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:11,760
the T helper cell via an
interaction between GP120

296
00:19:11,760 --> 00:19:15,680
and the CD4 receptor on
the T helper cell surface.

297
00:19:15,900 --> 00:19:18,200
This is shown on the top left.

298
00:19:18,500 --> 00:19:22,840
Once bound, a co-receptor on
the T helper cell membrane,

299
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:28,220
CCR5, binds the GP120
-CD4 complex to cause a

300
00:19:28,220 --> 00:19:32,580
conformational change in
GP120, allowing it to first

301
00:19:32,580 --> 00:19:35,640
insert itself into the T
cell membrane and then fold

302
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:39,440
back on itself, approximating
the viral and cell

303
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:44,360
membranes resulting in membrane
fusion. The ***** capsid

304
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:47,320
enters the cytoplasm,
and while traveling along

305
00:19:47,320 --> 00:19:51,440
microtubules, the reverse
transcriptase is activated,

306
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:55,560
transcribes first a negative
-sense DNA strand, denatures

307
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:59,060
the viral RNA, and then
reverse transcribes the DNA

308
00:19:59,060 --> 00:20:03,000
strand to form a double
-stranded DNA viral genome.

309
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:07,160
Viral integrase attaches
to and facilitates the

310
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:10,140
migration of the viral
DNA through a nuclear pore

311
00:20:10,140 --> 00:20:14,720
and integrates it into
the host genome. At that

312
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:20,380
point, the viral genome
is called a provirus as it

313
00:20:20,380 --> 00:20:24,140
is integrated into the
host DNA and it can remain

314
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:29,180
latent for days, weeks,
years, and even longer.

315
00:20:30,670 --> 00:20:34,920
At some point in the future,
cellular RNA polymerase

316
00:20:34,920 --> 00:20:38,360
transcribes the integrated
viral genome to produce

317
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:42,140
viral RNA that migrates to
the cytoplasm and is either

318
00:20:42,140 --> 00:20:45,200
translated on ribosomes to
produce the viral proteins

319
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:49,180
and enzymes or are
incorporated into assembling

320
00:20:49,180 --> 00:20:53,740
viral capsids. Once assembled,
the capsid abuts the

321
00:20:53,740 --> 00:20:56,300
inner surface of the cell
membrane and buds from the

322
00:20:56,300 --> 00:21:00,120
cell to be surrounded by
the lipid bilayer envelope.

323
00:21:00,780 --> 00:21:04,900
Throughout this slide,
you see in red the names

324
00:21:04,900 --> 00:21:09,460
of antiretrovirals and at
which points they act in

325
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:12,360
the life cycle. You'll
learn a lot more about

326
00:21:12,360 --> 00:21:16,240
these during your pharmacology
lecture on antiretroviral

327
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:19,620
therapy, and we'll
talk a little bit more

328
00:21:19,620 --> 00:21:23,800
about antiretrovirals to
some extent down the line.

329
00:21:24,260 --> 00:21:27,300
There is one I'd like
to point out on this

330
00:21:27,300 --> 00:21:30,800
slide, and at the top
left, that is Moraviroc.

331
00:21:31,220 --> 00:21:39,480
Moraviroc acts to prevent
CCR5 from binding with GP120

332
00:21:39,480 --> 00:21:45,900
and the CD4 receptor. This
prevents HIV from being

333
00:21:45,900 --> 00:21:49,200
able to enter the T helper
cell in the first place.

334
00:21:50,130 --> 00:21:53,880
CCR5 is thought to be the
co-receptor on T helper

335
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:59,200
cells in just about every
newly infected person,

336
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:04,220
but in some people over
time, that co-receptor

337
00:22:04,220 --> 00:22:07,710
may switch to another
molecule called CXCR4.

338
00:22:08,740 --> 00:22:15,100
And in those persons, HIV
evolves to use CXCR4 as a co

339
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:19,680
-receptor. And in some people,
it becomes a mix of CCR5

340
00:22:19,680 --> 00:22:25,480
and CXCR4, and those are
termed dual tropic viruses.

341
00:22:25,480 --> 00:22:30,060
The point is, in those
persons who have either

342
00:22:30,060 --> 00:22:35,120
a mix or solely CXCR4
as the co-receptor,

343
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:38,840
Meraviroc no longer works.
We'll talk even more

344
00:22:38,840 --> 00:22:43,780
about CCR5 when we talk
about possible cures for HIV.

345
00:23:09,400 --> 00:23:11,660
Here is a scheme of the
time course of someone

346
00:23:11,660 --> 00:23:14,560
who is infected with HIV
who does not get treated.

347
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:16,500
This is something we
hope doesn't happen

348
00:23:16,500 --> 00:23:18,460
today, but it was
typical of most

349
00:23:18,460 --> 00:23:20,920
patients prior to
antiretroviral therapy.

350
00:23:21,260 --> 00:23:24,460
The graph is divided into
three sections. As we

351
00:23:24,460 --> 00:23:26,940
review these sections,
focus your attention on

352
00:23:26,940 --> 00:23:31,220
the curves showing the CD8
or cytotoxic T cell and

353
00:23:31,220 --> 00:23:36,480
CD4 or T helper cell counts,
the anti-HIV antibody,

354
00:23:36,480 --> 00:23:40,620
and HIV viral load. The
HIV viral load is the

355
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:44,220
number of viral genomes
per mil or milliliter.

356
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:47,380
First, there is acute
infection followed

357
00:23:47,380 --> 00:23:50,860
very shortly by acute
retroviral syndrome.

358
00:23:51,260 --> 00:23:53,120
After acute infection,

359
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:57,080
progenitors of activated
T helper cells do a fairly

360
00:23:57,080 --> 00:24:00,400
good job of replenishing the
T helper cell population,

361
00:24:00,400 --> 00:24:04,520
allowing there to be some
humoral and cytotoxic T

362
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:09,120
cell control of HIV infection,
causing there to be a

363
00:24:09,120 --> 00:24:13,480
prolonged period of asymptomatic
or latent infection.

364
00:24:13,730 --> 00:24:17,740
There are, however, millions
of T helper cells that

365
00:24:17,740 --> 00:24:21,020
are being destroyed by the
infection every day, and

366
00:24:21,020 --> 00:24:24,840
at some threshold,
replenishing just can't keep

367
00:24:24,840 --> 00:24:28,120
up. As you've learned in
other lectures, the T helper

368
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:32,440
cell is a critical participant
in both humoral and

369
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:36,880
cell-mediated immunity.
Thus, as the CD4 cell count

370
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:41,480
decreases below 200, both
humoral and cell-mediated

371
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:45,280
immunity rapidly begin
to fail, and by the time

372
00:24:45,280 --> 00:24:49,360
CD4 cell counts are very
low, say the single digits,

373
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:51,720
death usually ensues from an

374
00:24:51,720 --> 00:24:54,280
opportunistic infection
or malignancy.

375
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,850
Let's look at each
one of these sections

376
00:25:03,850 --> 00:25:05,390
of the time course
individually.

377
00:25:05,490 --> 00:25:09,010
Two to four weeks after
acute HIV infection, many

378
00:25:09,010 --> 00:25:12,030
persons experience acute
retroviral syndrome.

379
00:25:12,210 --> 00:25:15,790
This occurs because HIV
migrates through the blood

380
00:25:15,790 --> 00:25:18,790
to regional nodes to
infect dendritic cells,

381
00:25:18,790 --> 00:25:22,190
another cell type that
expresses the CD4 receptor.

382
00:25:22,710 --> 00:25:25,490
Viral replication explodes and

383
00:25:25,490 --> 00:25:27,590
billions of copies
are produced.

384
00:25:27,870 --> 00:25:31,070
This results in a
very high viral RNA

385
00:25:31,070 --> 00:25:33,970
and an acute drop
in CD4 cell count.

386
00:25:33,970 --> 00:25:37,510
Some persons actually experience
mild immune deficiency

387
00:25:37,510 --> 00:25:40,950
during acute retroviral
syndrome that manifests as

388
00:25:40,950 --> 00:25:45,590
oropharyngeal or vaginal
candidiasis. There is also a

389
00:25:45,590 --> 00:25:49,990
vigorous humoral response,
so patients may have fever,

390
00:25:49,990 --> 00:25:54,810
fatigue, and often experience
a non-exudative pharyngitis,

391
00:25:54,810 --> 00:25:58,910
lymphadenitis, rash,
headache, aseptic meningitis,

392
00:25:59,450 --> 00:26:03,170
nausea, and diarrhea. The
illness lasts a couple

393
00:26:03,170 --> 00:26:05,730
of weeks or so, although
there can be prolonged

394
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:09,430
fatigue. An important
point is that the astute

395
00:26:09,430 --> 00:26:12,730
clinician who sees a person
with risk factors and what

396
00:26:12,730 --> 00:26:16,830
appears to be a viral
illness will have a high

397
00:26:16,830 --> 00:26:19,770
index of suspicion for
acute retroviral syndrome.

398
00:26:19,890 --> 00:26:22,910
Making that diagnosis and
placing the patient on

399
00:26:22,910 --> 00:26:27,130
antiretroviral therapy this
early in infection usually

400
00:26:27,130 --> 00:26:30,250
results in excellent
outcomes for the patient.

401
00:26:38,980 --> 00:26:43,440
The asymptomatic or latent
period of infection lasts

402
00:26:43,440 --> 00:26:47,200
on average about 8 to
10 years. There is a lot

403
00:26:47,200 --> 00:26:50,620
going on during this period.
First, in the United States,

404
00:26:50,620 --> 00:26:54,260
about 1 in 7 persons who
are infected don't know

405
00:26:54,260 --> 00:26:56,880
it. There is a lot of
transmission during the latent

406
00:26:56,880 --> 00:27:00,360
period. As we said
before, progenitors try to

407
00:27:00,360 --> 00:27:05,300
replete the CD4 cell count
as HIV is killing millions

408
00:27:05,300 --> 00:27:08,560
of CD4 cells every day,
but the CD4 cell count

409
00:27:08,560 --> 00:27:13,060
progressively declines and
the HIV viral load, the RNA,

410
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:17,120
continues to increase.
However, it is this prolonged

411
00:27:17,120 --> 00:27:22,040
period of immune activation
that results in metabolic

412
00:27:22,040 --> 00:27:25,140
abnormalities increasing
the risk of cardiovascular

413
00:27:25,140 --> 00:27:29,360
and renal disease, the metabolic
syndrome, hyperlipidemia,

414
00:27:29,360 --> 00:27:33,200
fat redistribution, and
metabolic acidosis. Toward

415
00:27:33,200 --> 00:27:36,280
the end of the latent
phase, some patients will

416
00:27:36,280 --> 00:27:40,780
experience some constitutional
symptoms such as fatigue,

417
00:27:40,980 --> 00:27:45,040
weight loss, or even
occasional fever. And lastly,

418
00:27:45,040 --> 00:27:49,320
throughout this time, the
progressive loss of CD4

419
00:27:49,320 --> 00:27:53,940
cells and humoral immunity
results in progressively

420
00:27:53,950 --> 00:27:57,540
increasing holes in the
immune system. We used to call

421
00:27:57,540 --> 00:28:01,120
these immune lacunae. For
example, someone who has

422
00:28:01,120 --> 00:28:05,620
previously vaccinated for
streptococcus pneumoniae may

423
00:28:05,620 --> 00:28:08,460
completely lose that
immunity gained from the

424
00:28:08,460 --> 00:28:13,020
vaccine. How many and which
immune lacunae occur in

425
00:28:13,020 --> 00:28:17,220
different patients is
unpredictable, but the lacunae do

426
00:28:17,220 --> 00:28:21,240
increase the risk of
infections for the patient. The

427
00:28:28,040 --> 00:28:32,180
final phase of untreated
HIV infection is the

428
00:28:32,180 --> 00:28:36,520
symptomatic phase. CD4
drops below 200 and finally

429
00:28:36,520 --> 00:28:40,220
below 100 and into the
single digits. This results

430
00:28:40,220 --> 00:28:44,140
in a severe immune
suppression that in a

431
00:28:44,140 --> 00:28:47,100
stepwise manner increases
the risk of certain

432
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:49,980
opportunistic infections
and malignancies. There is

433
00:28:49,980 --> 00:28:53,720
actually an increase in the
incidence of tuberculosis

434
00:28:53,720 --> 00:28:57,780
and lymphoma below a
CD4 cell count of 350.

435
00:28:57,780 --> 00:29:02,440
below 200, there is increased
risk for pneumocystis

436
00:29:02,440 --> 00:29:06,480
urovicii, below 100, cerebral
toxoplasmosis, and below

437
00:29:06,480 --> 00:29:11,520
50, CMV retinitis,
disseminated CMV, cryptococcal

438
00:29:11,520 --> 00:29:15,180
meningitis, esophageal
candidiasis, and disseminated

439
00:29:15,180 --> 00:29:19,720
Mycobacterium avium
intracellulari complex. AIDS is

440
00:29:19,720 --> 00:29:25,420
defined as anyone who has a
CD4 count less than 200 or

441
00:29:25,420 --> 00:29:30,800
a CD4 percentage of less
than 14, but also when anyone

442
00:29:30,800 --> 00:29:35,180
of any cell count or CD4
cell count has an AIDS

443
00:29:35,180 --> 00:29:39,700
-defining illness, including
CMV retinitis, pneumocystis,

444
00:29:39,700 --> 00:29:43,640
and the other conditions
shown above, period. There

445
00:29:43,640 --> 00:29:46,780
are also malignancies that
are AIDS-defining illnesses,

446
00:29:46,780 --> 00:29:50,280
including CNS lymphoma,
Kaposi's sarcoma, and

447
00:29:50,280 --> 00:29:54,140
cervical cancer. Advanced
HIV also increases the risk

448
00:29:54,140 --> 00:29:57,200
of other malignancies, such
as Hodgkin's disease, oral

449
00:29:57,200 --> 00:30:00,980
cavity or pharyngeal
carcinoma, ****, liver, and

450
00:30:00,980 --> 00:30:04,900
lung cancer. A link to the
current list of AIDS-defining

451
00:30:04,900 --> 00:30:08,540
illnesses is at the bottom
of this slide, period.

452
00:30:09,360 --> 00:30:12,770
And with that information,
Bobby is understandably

453
00:30:12,770 --> 00:30:15,560
concerned. He agrees to
HIV testing, which is

454
00:30:15,560 --> 00:30:18,460
positive. You counsel him,
understand how upset he

455
00:30:18,460 --> 00:30:21,620
must be, and how worried
he is. You let him know

456
00:30:21,620 --> 00:30:23,780
that with the current
treatment, he can expect to

457
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:26,820
live a very long life
if he is compliant. You

458
00:30:26,820 --> 00:30:29,760
recommend that he use 100
% barrier protection during

459
00:30:29,760 --> 00:30:32,380
***, and you let him know
that you need to order

460
00:30:32,380 --> 00:30:35,040
some more blood tests.
What tests would you order?

461
00:30:41,950 --> 00:30:45,910
We ordered the state-of-the
-art HIV test, the fourth

462
00:30:45,910 --> 00:30:50,350
-generation antigen antibody
assay that tests for p24

463
00:30:50,350 --> 00:30:54,590
antigen and anti-HIV antibody.
You will remember that

464
00:30:54,590 --> 00:30:58,110
p24 is the capsid protein
coded for by the GAG gene.

465
00:30:58,110 --> 00:31:00,650
It is generally detectable
in blood somewhere between

466
00:31:00,650 --> 00:31:03,710
two and three weeks after
infection. Previous diagnostic

467
00:31:03,710 --> 00:31:07,250
testing relied solely on
anti-HIV antibodies that

468
00:31:07,250 --> 00:31:10,610
weren't detectable for up
to 12 weeks after infection.

469
00:31:10,610 --> 00:31:14,190
So the inclusion of p24
antigen testing, significantly

470
00:31:14,190 --> 00:31:18,170
reduces the length of the
window period, the duration

471
00:31:18,170 --> 00:31:21,910
between infection and
detection of infection with

472
00:31:21,910 --> 00:31:24,990
a positive test. That window
period is about two weeks

473
00:31:24,990 --> 00:31:28,090
now, but even if the
fourth generation test is

474
00:31:28,090 --> 00:31:31,370
negative or indeterminate,
if there is a high index of

475
00:31:31,370 --> 00:31:34,950
suspicion, it is recommended
to perform a nucleic acid

476
00:31:34,950 --> 00:31:39,090
amplification test, such
as an HIV viral load by PCR

